Alembic migration environment — Career Coach Agent v2
=====================================================

Async SQLAlchemy migrations for the Postgres schema (design §4 / §8).

Layout
------
  backend/
    alembic.ini                     # config; run alembic from backend/ (its cwd)
    migrations/
      env.py                        # async env; reads DATABASE_URL from app.config.Settings
      script.py.mako                # migration file template
      init/01_enable_pgvector.sql   # P0-07: enables the `vector` extension (NOT Alembic)
      versions/                     # migration scripts (0001_baseline is a no-op)

Connection config
-----------------
`env.py` injects `sqlalchemy.url` from `app.config.Settings.DATABASE_URL` — the same
settings object the app uses — so Alembic and the app never drift. There is no URL in
`alembic.ini`. Running any alembic command therefore needs the app's env vars set
(`DATABASE_URL`, plus the other required settings). Locally these come from the root
`.env`; in containers from compose / HF Space Secrets.

pgvector extension
------------------
The `vector` extension is created once by `init/01_enable_pgvector.sql`, which the
Postgres container runs on first init (before Alembic). Do NOT `CREATE EXTENSION` in an
Alembic migration — assume it already exists.

Common commands (run from `backend/`)
-------------------------------------
  alembic upgrade head            # apply all migrations
  alembic downgrade -1            # revert the last migration
  alembic downgrade base          # revert everything
  alembic current                 # show the applied revision
  alembic history                 # list revisions
  alembic revision -m "add users" --autogenerate   # generate from ORM models

In Docker / compose (explicit, separate from app startup):
  docker compose run --rm backend alembic upgrade head

Migrations are never auto-run from the FastAPI lifespan — schema management is an
explicit, operator-driven step, kept distinct from the app's runtime connection pool.
